{
  "summary": "This scan found three items, none of which proves anything is wrong, but they are worth a quick check together. Two remote-control programs (AnyDesk and TeamViewer) are installed, and there is an extra administrator account. First confirm that you or someone you trust installed both remote-access programs; then confirm you recognize the <account-2> account.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "title": "Two remote-control programs are installed (AnyDesk and TeamViewer)",
      "finding_ids": [
        "REMOTE-ACCESS-TOOL:c226f725",
        "REMOTE-ACCESS-TOOL:1ba22cd3"
      ],
      "explanation": "AnyDesk is set up as a background service, and TeamViewer is set to start automatically when you sign in. Both let someone see and control this computer from another location. That is normal if you use them yourself or a family member or IT helper set them up. If you don't remember installing them, take them seriously: scammers often ask people to install exactly these tools, and they can stay as a way back in. Having two such tools at once is worth noticing. If you don't use one or both, the report shows how to deal with each finding."
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "title": "An extra administrator account exists",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:fde0b291"
      ],
      "explanation": "The account <computer>\\<account-2> has full control of this computer. Many people keep a separate admin account on purpose, which is good practice, so this is often harmless. If you don't recognize it, especially alongside the remote-access tools above, it could be a sign someone set up their own way in. Check that you know who created it; the report shows what to do if you don't."
    }
  ],
